<article class="env-remark" id="0727">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0727">Remark <span data-tag="0727">9.7.7.13</span> <span class="named">(The Pentagon Identity)</span>.</a> To simplify notation, let us write $\otimes $ for the $\mathbb {K}$-cocomplete tensor product $\otimes _{\mathbb {K}}$. If $\operatorname{\mathcal{B}}$, $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$, and $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$ are $\mathbb {K}$-cocomplete $\infty $-categories, then the diagram of equivalences </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@C =-30pt@R=30pt{ &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{B}}\otimes ((\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\otimes \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}) \otimes \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}) \ar [rr]^-{ \alpha _{\operatorname{\mathcal{B}}, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\otimes \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}, \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}} } &amp;  &amp;  (\operatorname{\mathcal{B}}\otimes (\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\otimes \operatorname{\mathcal{D}})) \otimes \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\ar [dr]^{ \alpha _{\operatorname{\mathcal{B}}, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}, \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}} \otimes \operatorname{id}} &amp;  \\ \operatorname{\mathcal{B}}\otimes (\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\otimes (\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}\otimes \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}) ) \ar [ur]^{ \operatorname{id}\otimes \alpha _{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}},\operatorname{\mathcal{D}},\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}} } \ar [drr]_{ \alpha _{\operatorname{\mathcal{B}},\operatorname{\mathcal{C}},\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}\otimes \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}}} &amp;  &amp;  &amp;  &amp;  ((\operatorname{\mathcal{B}}\otimes \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) \otimes \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}) \otimes \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\\ &amp;  &amp;  (\operatorname{\mathcal{B}}\otimes \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) \otimes (\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}\otimes \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}) \ar [urr]_{\alpha _{ \operatorname{\mathcal{B}}\otimes \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}, \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}, \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}} } &amp;  &amp;  } \]
</div>
<p> commutes up to isomorphism. To prove this, let $F$ and $G$ denote the equivalences given by clockwise and counterclockwise composition around the diagram, and consider the functor </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  T: \operatorname{\mathcal{B}}\times \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\times \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}\times \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{B}}\otimes (\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\otimes (\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}\otimes \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}) ) \quad \quad (B,C,D,E) \mapsto B \otimes (C \otimes (D \otimes E) ). \]
</div>
<p> Applying Corollary <a data-tag="0725" href="/tag/0725">9.7.7.11</a> twice, we see that $T$ exhibits $\operatorname{\mathcal{B}}\otimes (\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\otimes (\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}\otimes \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}) )$ as a tensor product of the collection $\{  \operatorname{\mathcal{B}}, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}, \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}, \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\} $. Consequently, to show that the $\mathbb {K}$-cocontinuous functors $F$ and $G$ are isomorphic, it will suffice to show that the $\mathbb {K}$-multilinear functors </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  (F \circ T), (G \circ T): \operatorname{\mathcal{B}}\times \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\times \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}\times \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\rightarrow ( (\operatorname{\mathcal{B}}\otimes \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) \otimes \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}) \otimes \operatorname{\mathcal{E}} \]
</div>
<p> are isomorphic. This is clear, since both are isomorphic to the functor $(B,C,D,E) \mapsto ((B \otimes C) \otimes D) \otimes E$. </p>
</article>
